description:
In crates/reader/src/main.rs (around line 344-349), the drain timeout arm re-queries semaphore_drain.available_permits() after the timeout has already fired:

    Err(_) => {
        let remaining = max_connections - semaphore_drain.available_permits();
        warn!(remaining_connections = remaining, "drain timeout exceeded");
        std::process::exit(1);
    }

Between the timeout expiring and this re-query, additional sessions may
have released permits, so the logged remaining_connections can be lower
than the actual count at timeout — potentially even zero, which would
produce a misleading 'timed out with 0 connections remaining' log line.

Fix: capture the remaining count before entering the timeout future, or
accept the count is approximate and note it in the log message. The
warning message should make clear it is a snapshot count at timeout, not
a precise count.
